WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.012
Spark often uses lazy evaluation.

00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:10.297
That means many transformation steps describe what should happen without immediately processing the entire dataset.

00:00:10.297 --> 00:00:16.237
You might select a few columns, add a filter, and define another transformation.

00:00:16.237 --> 00:00:18.380
Spark can keep building the plan.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:23.836
The larger computation begins when an action needs an actual result.

00:00:23.836 --> 00:00:32.511
For example, displaying rows, counting records, collecting data, or writing a table can trigger execution.

00:00:32.511 --> 00:00:39.681
This is useful because Spark can examine several transformations together and optimize the combined work before running

00:00:39.681 --> 00:00:41.131
it.

00:00:41.131 --> 00:00:48.241
So when you write Spark code, remember that defining a transformation and actually executing the job are not always the

00:00:48.241 --> 00:00:50.106
same moment.
